  "articleBody": "Thinking about a garage door upgrade? It’s more than just picking a pretty door! You'll want to think about door size, of course, to make sure it fits your opening just right. Insulation is a big one, especially in Colorado's changing weather – a well-insulated door can really help with energy efficiency. Safety features are also crucial; look for things like auto-reverse mechanisms and photo eyes that stop the door if something’s in the way. Don’t forget about opener compatibility; your new door and existing opener need to play nice together, or it might be time for a new opener too. You should also consider whether an upgrade means new springs, tracks, sensors, and good weather sealing. These components all work together to determine how well your door performs and how long it lasts. It’s definitely worth considering the material (steel, wood, fiberglass) and its durability, how noisy it is, and its wind resistance. And of course, the warranty on the door and the installation itself. If you're feeling overwhelmed by all these choices, or if your upgrade involves electrical work or structural changes, it's a great time to call in the pros to ensure everything is installed safely and correctly.",
